Global measles deaths hit a historic low in 2025, the World Health Organization said on Friday, although millions of children ⁠still missed vaccinations and outbreaks persisted in dozens of countries. The UN health agency estimated 9.8 million measles cases and about 72,000 deaths worldwide in 2025 — down 74% from 37.8 million cases in 2000, with deaths falling roughly 91% from about 769,000.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a11fc-eb12-11f1-a67c-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261128-081831-082002-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c3a11fc-eb12-11f1-a67c-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261128-081831-082002-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">71573246-eb12-11f1-896a-575c3766f108</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:34:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Immigration, a key issue in Sunday's Spanish snap election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/immigration-a-key-issue-in-sunday-s-spanish-snap-election</link><description>
